  "reviewer_notes": "This is primarily a methodological/framework paper proposing a model for developing EnPIs in kraft pulp mills; it does not fit statistical energy models. Studied cases are three kraft pulp mills of one Swedish company group, treated here as a single multi-site application (A1) with a 'reference mill' and 'Mill 2' as the empirical contexts. Two energy performance indicators were treated as models: mill-level SEC (M1, an intensity ratio) and the evaporation steam-demand-per-kg-dry-solids indicator (M2, with numeric results in Table 3). Numeric steam-demand reductions in Table 3 are stated by the authors to be calculated/theoretical (85% evaporator efficiency assumed). Future-work statements (e.g. 'Further research is suggested ... in the form of case studies') were not recorded as limitations per instrument rules.",
